From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:29:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The nocked arrow points along the shot

The arrow on the string hand (HandArrow) turns to face a mark from its own
seat: our own hero's, while the aiming camera is up, the reticle's point;
everyone else's the bow's grip (HandLeft). 1.12's hold pose sets the string
hand's bone across the bow, and with the shoulders turned to the aim the
arrow lay sideways along the old stance. Riders take the turn in the rig
lane, a plain child of its bone's anchor under it.
